      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 106369928,
      "text": "ニューギニアインパチェンス はツリフネソウ科の多年生植物。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Impatiens hawkeri」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Impatiens_hawkeri",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1353318505,
      "text": "Impatiens hawkeri, the New Guinea impatiens, is a species of flowering plant in the family Balsaminaceae. It is native to Papua New Guinea and the Solomon Islands. It has been bred and hybridized in cultivation to produce a line of garden plants."
    }
  },
  "sections": {
    "cultivation": {
      "ja": {
        "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「ニューギニアインパチェンス」の節「育て方」",
        "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%83%8B%E3%83%A5%E3%83%BC%E3%82%AE%E3%83%8B%E3%82%A2%E3%82%A4%E3%83%B3%E3%83%91%E3%83%81%E3%82%A7%E3%83%B3%E3%82%B9#%E8%82%B2%E3%81%A6%E6%96%B9",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
        "revision": 106369928,
        "heading": "育て方",
        "text": "インパチェンスが花壇材料として生産され、取り扱われるのにたいして、ニューギニアインパチェンスは鉢植えとして生産、出荷される。夏に市場に出回る植物であるが、多年草で、10℃以上のところであれば越冬できる。冬季は霜の下りない室内などに取り込んで管理する。\n差し芽で増やすことができる。",
        "truncated": false
      },
      "en": {
        "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Impatiens hawkeri」の節「Cultivation」",
        "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Impatiens_hawkeri#Cultivation",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
        "revision": 1353318505,
        "heading": "Cultivation",
        "text": "It was first collected in the Territory of Papua in 1884 and soon became popular as a greenhouse plant. After its discovery, fifteen other similar New Guinea taxa were collected, all of which were later determined to be forms of I. hawkeri.\nPlants with a great variety of flower and leaf colours are sold in nurseries. The species has been crossed with Impatiens aurantiaca and I. platypetala to improve characteristics such as drought resistance.",
        "truncated": false
      }
    }
  },
